A||N||5||CoolBlue87GT||Speedvision Classics Roadshow Idea ....||||1||
Z||000000||CoolBlue87GT||12-28-2001||03:03 PM||||I've posted this in the general chat forum.<BR>Posting here to get the biggest responce.<P>I watched a Speedvision Classic Roadshow tonight on the Fords & Chevy cars.<P>Got an Idea, why not contact them & ask if they'd be interested in creating a show about the Fiero's<P><B>Maybe we all could send a request ???????</B><P>Here's their email address:<BR>Speedvision@CNS<P>Here's my message to them:<P>First I want to say thanks for the great programming Speedvision has produced. <P>The Classics Roadshow is the best. Just love those. <P>I know this E-mail is one among thousands you will receive. I hope & pray somehow this gets noticed.<P>My name is Dave Lambert, I live in Punta Gorda Florida. If you need to contact me, my number in (***) ***-**** (edited out)<P>I thank you in advance for even just reading this.<P>Was wondering is anyone has considered doing a show about the Pontiac Fiero.<P>It's the only / Best mid engine production sports car ever produced by an American<BR>car company from 1984 - 1988.<P>This is not a letter trying to 'show off" my car. I'm just trying to see if you might<BR>have any interest in creating a show based on these cars.<P>There is a huge following that this car still has. We all would love to see a show<BR>made about these models. We'd love to see all years & models shown.<P>I belong to a club that is world wide, named Pennocks Fiero Forum. There are hundreds of Fiero owners that visit this fantastic web site.<P>It was created and run by a gentleman, Cliff Pennock.<P>The internet address is  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/cgi-bin/fiero/Ultimate.cgi?action=intro" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/cgi-bin/fiero/Ultimate.cgi?action=intro</A>  <P>At the end of this message, I'll include a path where you can view more pic's of my car & other Fiero's at the Daytona show.<P>In March 2001, a National show was held inside the Daytona Speedway. Over 170 Fiero's<BR>were there in many different forms, Stock, modified, V8's ... on & on<P>My 87 Fiero GT w/ only 1700 miles was chosen Best of Stock, Best Stock Paint, & Best of Show !!!!!<P>(I enclosed a pic of my car here)<P>More information: <A HREF="http://communities.msn.com/SuncoastFieroClub/daytona2001.msnw" TARGET=_blank>http://communities.msn.com/SuncoastFieroClub/daytona2001.msnw</A>  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||CoolBlue87GT||12-28-2001||03:05 PM||||Message sent by [b]Cheever3000[b/]<BR>                 <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Excellent. I have often wished someone with resources would make a documentary on Fiero ownership, and all the colorful groups & personalities we know and love. This might be the closest we'll get to that. I'll be sending my email to them soon.<BR> ||||reg||4
Z||000002||CoolBlue87GT||12-28-2001||03:06 PM||||!!!!! Hey guy's !!!!<BR>I got a response back from Speedvision !!!<P>As follows :<P>From: Speedvision@CNS on 12/28/2001 02:05 PM<P><BR>Thank you for your comments and suggestions. I will forward your<BR>message along to our producers. They are very interested to know what and<BR>who our viewers like, dislike and what they would like to see more of.<P>Thank you for taking the time to write us and for watching Speedvision.<P>Sincerely,<BR>Program Services,<BR>Speedvision Network<P>-------------------------------------<P>Might not hurt to have more of us send your own email messages !!<P>What do ya think ???<P>||||reg||4
